WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.480
Rose of Passion

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.740
Isn't it your bedtime?

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.990
I won't lose!

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.240
Oh, I'm <i>so</i> scared.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.630
I feel like I'm going crazy

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.380
I like nice songs

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:39.850
and I want you to listen to them too

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.810
Whenever

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.480
I sing a song

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.070
I hear a voice coming from the microphone

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:56.490
wishing me the best

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:59.240
I want you

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:00.780
to hear it too

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.620
Good luck!

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.790
You can't show your love

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.290
just with niceties

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:16.170
That won't provide comfort

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.550
Whenever I say something

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.640
out of the ordinary

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.940
in my heart

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.440
I wish you the best

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.980
I want you

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.610
to hear that line

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:37.610
Good luck!

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.800
You're too stiff. You're leaving too many openings.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.060
You should relax more.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:21.240
I know that you're strong,

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.660
but I <i>cannot</i> lose to you.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.830
For everyone's sake...

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.750
For Mom's sake!

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:34.960
Chi!

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:38.080
Ossie!

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:45.830
What?!

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:46.350
Mr. Slo!

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:00.800
Go home.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.320
Go back to your poor, but peaceful life.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.000
Mom!

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.540
Let's go home, Momo.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.840
I did not teach you how to wield a sword for this.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.640
Move, Mom.

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:25.680
I have to defeat her...

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:29.930
Momo!

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.460
Are you okay, Momo?

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.690
Haru, why?

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.190
That's...

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.190
her mother.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.690
Huh?

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.920
She's not ready to know yet.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.500
<i>No, that's not it...</i>

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:01.180
<i>I just wanted to be her mother for a little longer.</i>

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:07.400
How do you do? It's been a while, Fujiwara Haru.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.680
So, that's your daughter?

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:13.360
She takes after her mother, it seems.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.660
It seems so.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:22.690
These dolls cannot harm anyone.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:27.960
They may look threatening, but they will not hurt you.

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:35.920
The state vigilante squad, the
Okayama Demons, is no more.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.820
<i>You</i> are the only one living in that castle.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:44.440
<i>You</i>, the Best who protected Okayama from the Hiroshima without honor and humanity,

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:49.600
who abused your authority to deceive the sovereign and bully the citizens.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.480
I'll have the reasons for thy betrayal, Kukino Ura!

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:00.000
You're so old-fashioned, as usual!

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.320
Perhaps this is an appropriate response.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:08.060
Don't waste thy breath!

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:27.680
Excuse me, Kaguya!

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.600
There's a visitor from Okayama.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:40.860
He's looking for Fuhito.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.480
Okayama?

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:44.860
If he's looking for Kuramochi,
he's in the hospital.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:46.860
It sounds like it's important!

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.880
Are you... going to get back at them?

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.680
You can't do that!

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:05.200
You're just a substitute peacebroker, right?
Why are you trying so hard?

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.510
I don't like it!

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:09.940
I... just don't.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:14.680
It doesn't matter if I'm a substitute or a Best...

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.600
I may just be a meddling outsider,

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:21.340
but I can't leave it alone!

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.780
I am the former captain of the Okayama Demons.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:32.660
My name is Kibino.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:37.540
A secret agreement between Hiroshima and Okayama?

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:43.630
She chose to protect her country, and thus take on
its citizens' hate, rather than watch its destruction.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:49.130
Kukino Ura dismissed her squad and became the demon she is now.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.880
However, that charade has also reached its limit.

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:55.900
If Mr. Kuramochi makes everything known to the public,

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:59.760
not for retribution, but for justice,

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.350
he could then take care of the rest by himself.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:06.110
Ishizukuri is from a former branch family line.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:09.400
If Okayama acknowledges the secret agreement,

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.360
then the former head family will bring about justice.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:16.800
Yes. However, the captain does not agree with me.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:19.080
Now that the citizens are starting an uprising,

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:24.080
I thought I would try to convince
Mr. Kuramochi and ask for his help.

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:28.090
Kuramochi never said a word about that...

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:30.780
He's always like that,

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:34.090
hiding everything behind his wide back.

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:37.470
Aren't I a member of the main family too?

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:42.000
Let us go.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.840
It's time to bring about justice.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:54.100
The captain over there's Momo's mom?

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:56.000
What's going on?

00:07:57.460 --> 00:07:59.620
The president never had any time

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:05.170
because she was doing everything she could to return you to your real family.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:07.420
<i>Real</i> family?

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.040
Then, what's Mom?

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:15.050
Your mom is still your mom.

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:18.050
That's right.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:27.650
Both of them are her mom, right?

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.680
Yeah...

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:32.150
Yeah!

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:34.740
I'm gonna borrow this for a sec, Momo!

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:40.080
