00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:48.580
Hey, about that stone.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:49.920
Oh, that's right!

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:51.880
Huh?

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:56.420
I've held onto this the whole time, yet I didn't become a Best once!

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:58.900
Yeah, me neither!

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:01.980
Those stones are really...

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:05.300
Is that Yukippe?

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:06.680
Huh?

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.500
Mr. Kuramochi?!

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:14.420
Hey, don't tell me you have no sense of direction...

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:17.340
No, it's not that I have no sense of direction...

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:20.780
Did you really come this way?

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:23.260
Wh-Why don't we take a break?

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:25.080
Answer the question!

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:37.710
I cannot overlook the fact that you forced Okayama's Best

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:40.920
to make her citizens suffer for your sake!

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:42.890
As the successor to the main family,

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:45.470
I demand that you apologize and return their money!

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:50.180
You must also relinquish the state vigilante squad license to the head of state!

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:52.980
I refuse!

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:57.860
Hiroshima was once undivided.

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:01.060
The main family and branch families and respectable folks...

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:05.260
They were coarse, but well-meaning people.

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:07.990
Ishizukuri Shima, you were, too!

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:09.820
What are you talking about?

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:12.980
I have a memory, ever so faint,

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:16.320
where you and I were havin' the time of our lives.

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:18.510
Can't recall.

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:22.120
The main family, the branch families, the respectable people?

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:28.890
Do you know how much those "well-meaning people" cared about us after we were ruined by bickering?

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:33.020
We were <i>nothing</i> to them!

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:40.530
And so you do <i>this</i>?

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.700
What are you trying to do?

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:48.980
Try starting a massive brawl with guys used to little skirmishes in their neck of the woods.

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:50.620
It just won't work.

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:55.630
First, I'll have Okonomiyaki Village

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:58.040
devour this archipelago without honor and humanity!

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:23.860
We take care of our own.

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:26.520
Everyone else can fend for themselves.

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:28.950
I know most people think like that, but...

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.080
it's not everyone!

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:36.160
There are still people that help those in need of help,

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:39.200
asking only for a little stone in return.

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:41.980
People that haven't given up on—

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:44.220
Well, they're idiots!

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:48.600
What are you doing?!

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:51.600
I have no use for moldy scraps of paper.

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:54.100
What I really wanted was...

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:02.660
Did the main family not tell their precious little girl anything?

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:09.320
During the clash of the twin towers in the Great Tokyo War,

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:15.080
there was a robot with specs that surpassed those of the Tokyo Tower Robot and the Tokyo Skytree Robot!

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:17.330
The chivalrous robot,

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.830
Daimon!

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:25.880
Miss Shima, the preparations are completed!

00:21:26.240 --> 00:21:28.460
Shigyo!

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:30.200
It looks like the ship has been completed!

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:32.220
We're halfway through!

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:36.040
Now we need to take over the ship and grab Otonashi.

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:38.770
Next time, make sure to push this button!

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:48.660
Good work. Next, why don't I have you mass produce this robot, then.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:54.660
If you want the Takumi-za sacred object that you brought out during the turmoil,

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:57.000
you'll know what to do.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:03.420
Now, get out of the way!

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:10.240
It's time for the fall of Hiroshima's false chivalry!

00:22:12.920 --> 00:22:14.100
Chivalrous...

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:15.000
Robot...

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:16.560
Daimon?

00:22:16.900 --> 00:22:19.160
It was made when Hiroshima was facing a crisis,

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:23.060
to be piloted by successors to the Nayotake name.

00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:25.800
I heard that in the confusion of the family war,

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:30.960
it was stolen from the main family storehouse by the Abe branch family, then the Isonokami family stole it,

00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:35.480
and then it finally ended up in the hands of Ishizukuri Shima.

00:22:35.480 --> 00:22:38.580
However, it will not move by itself.

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:42.320
That's probably why they wanted the license.

00:22:43.400 --> 00:22:46.590
If she rushed in to where the enemy is, then around now...

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:48.660
You said your name was Nozomi?

00:22:48.660 --> 00:22:50.220
Y-Yes.

00:22:50.220 --> 00:22:55.220
Will you bring this to the young lady... to Nayotake Kaguya?

00:22:59.280 --> 00:23:00.660
Takoyaki?

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:17.490
Thou shalt not pass

00:23:17.780 --> 00:23:22.870
Laws, reason, nobody is getting past

00:23:23.200 --> 00:23:28.710
I don't care what you say

00:23:28.710 --> 00:23:34.170
I'm not letting friends and lovers in either

00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:38.300
My only companion

00:23:39.640 --> 00:23:44.060
is the faint moonlight

00:23:45.140 --> 00:23:55.990
I'm now sitting in the cockpit

00:23:56.240 --> 00:24:02.240
of the black shadow

00:24:02.240 --> 00:24:05.870
deep in the white moon

00:24:07.040 --> 00:24:12.920
Of the black shadow

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:16.760
deep in the white moon

00:24:28.980 --> 00:24:31.900
You've probably already realized, but this show is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to real people, groups, or laws is coincidental.
